<title>UK: SIG half year pretax profit gains.</title>
<headline>SIG half year pretax profit gains.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.6		    vs 10.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.4		    vs 2.2</p>
<p> Pretax		     14.21		  vs 12.05</p>
<p> Turnover		   200.78		 vs 176.02</p>
<p> Operating result	 14.46		  vs 12.75</p>
<p> Interest		   0.67		   vs 0.69</p>
<p> Tax			  5.13		   vs 4.07</p>
<p> Net taxed		  9.09		   vs 7.96</p>
<p> Retained profit	  6.31		   vs 6.34</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 15</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 8</p>
<p>NOTE - Insulation product distributor SIG Group Plc chief executive Bill Forrester said in his results statement, &quot;trading in the last two months has been satisfactory,&quot; and that he viewed &quot;the second half and beyond with confidence.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
